      <h2>Short bio for event programs</h2>
      <p>
        Armağan Amcalar is the founder of Coyotiv, a Berlin software company and engineering school, and the CTO of OpenServ and Neol. A software architect with a
        background in electronics and brain research, he is the author of Gea Stack, a TypeScript-to-native compiler and UI framework, and of cote, a Node.js
        library for zero-configuration microservices. He previously led engineering at unu and Wayfair. He is a regular conference speaker, a lecturer, and the
        founder of Lonca, a software craftsmanship school for women engineers.
      </p>

